That confirms it — `.next` isn't listed, which is why the build cache (with your key baked in) got committed. Here's an updated `.gitignore` using Next.js's standard template, so you don't hit this with other generated folders either:

```gitignore
# dependencies
node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.js

# next.js
.next
/out

# production
/build

# env files
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
```
